// which defaults to `center center` and clips edges when the container
// aspect ratio differs from the source (most acutely on mobile, where the
// photo strip is ~200px tall against a 3:4 portrait source). Override per
// portrait so the subject's face stays in frame. Any CSS `object-position`
// value works: "center top", "50% 20%", "50% 25%", etc. When adding a new
// testimonial photo, add an entry here; otherwise the default applies.
const TESTIMONIAL_CROP_DEFAULT = 'center center';
