---

<style is:global>
  /* ─── FAQ accordion animation ──────────────────────────────────────── */
  details > .faq-body { animation: faqOpen 0.18s ease; }
  @keyframes faqOpen {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(-3px); }
    to   { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }

  /* ─── H2 accent line ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .h2-accent {
    display: block;
    width: 4rem;
    height: 1px;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    background: rgba(212, 169, 92, 0.55);  /* #D4A95C, saturated gold */
  }
  /* Darker variant on the pale Register 3 backgrounds for contrast */
  .sg-r3 .h2-accent {
    background: rgba(168, 124, 53, 0.7);   /* #A87C35, gold-dark for light bg */
  }

  /* ─── Section transitions ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
  /* Gradient bleed: dark → pale-R3 transitions feel gradual at the entry */
  .sg-r3-entry::before {
    content: '';
    display: block;
    height: 60px;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(7, 11, 20, 0.08), transparent);
    margin-bottom: -60px;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }
  /* Thin gold seam above certain sections to signal deliberate register change */
  .sg-seam-top {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(180, 140, 80, 0.18);
  }

  /* ─── Swiper: base overrides ────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sg-swiper {
    overflow: hidden;
    width: 100%;
  }
  /* Equal-height slides */
  .sg-swiper .swiper-wrapper {
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  .sg-swiper .swiper-slide {
    height: auto;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  .sg-swiper .sg-slide {
    height: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  /* ─── Swiper: disabled nav button ─────────────────────────────────── */
  .sg-nav-btn.swiper-button-disabled {
    opacity: 0.15 !important;
    cursor: not-allowed;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* ─── Swiper: pagination bullets (Sangham brand) ─────────────────── */
  /* Larger, more visible dots */
  .sg-pag .swiper-pagination-bullet {
    width: 10px !important;
    height: 10px !important;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.45);
    opacity: 1;
    margin: 0 6px !important;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: inline-block;
    vertical-align: middle;
    transition: width 0.22s ease, height 0.22s ease, background 0.22s ease, opacity 0.22s ease;
  }
  .sg-pag .swiper-pagination-bullet:hover {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
  }
  .sg-pag .swiper-pagination-bullet-active {
    width: 1.25rem !important;
    height: 10px !important;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: rgba(180, 140, 80, 0.85) !important;
    opacity: 1 !important;
  }
  /* Adequate tap target via parent padding */
  .sg-pag {
    padding: 8px 0;
  }

  /* ─── Cal.com inline embed containers ──────────────────────────────────
     Defensive sizing so the embed never collapses on mobile. Cal.com's
     embed.js injects an iframe at runtime; if the parent has min-height: 0
     the iframe renders 0px tall and looks like a missing calendar. Mobile
     gets the larger min-height because the month grid stacks vertically. */
  #cal-parental-embed,
  #cal-fit-embed {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 700px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    #cal-parental-embed,
    #cal-fit-embed {
      min-height: 650px;
    }
  }
  #cal-parental-embed iframe,
  #cal-fit-embed iframe {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    border: 0;
  }

  /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     READABILITY / CONTRAST PASS (B1-B6), scoped to this page only
     Targets the 50-65 parental demographic on mobile; lifts base luminance,
     cools and brightens text, increases minimum type sizes, and saturates
     gold for pull statements only. Site-wide tokens untouched.
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

  /* B1 - lighter dark base. Redefined inside .m-page so site-wide tokens
     are untouched. void becomes a softer blue-grey; header lifts to a
     slightly-paler variant for the existing "two-tier dark" rhythm. */
  .m-page {
    --color-void: hsl(218 32% 15%);            /* ~ #1A2333 */
    --color-header: hsl(217 26% 22%);          /* ~ #2A364B */
    --color-parchment: hsl(220 18% 93%);       /* ~ #E8EBF1, cool off-white */
    --color-header-foreground: hsl(220 18% 93%);

    /* E1 - gold token unification (page-scoped). Eliminates the muted
       brand gold (hsl(42 52% 42%) ~ #A67E36) and the pale gold-light
       (hsl(42 50% 52%) ~ #C29A53) that were appearing simultaneously
       on the page. Single saturated value used everywhere; hover state
       derived ~12% brighter; dark variant for borders. Button text
       contract flips to dark (foreground) so cream-on-saturated-gold
       contrast (~1.9:1, fails AA) becomes dark-on-saturated-gold
       (~6.7:1, AA pass) on every CTA. */
    --color-primary: #D4A95C;
    --color-primary-foreground: #0F1422;
    --color-gold: #D4A95C;
    --color-gold-light: #E6BE76;
    --color-gold-dark: #B88A3C;
  }

  /* B1 - overlay opacities on image-background sections. The dark overlays
     used to sit at 72-96%; with the lighter base the 96% felt nearly black.
     Soften by a few points so the image still anchors but doesn't crush. */
  .m-page .sg-overlay-strong { background-color: rgb(15 20 32 / 0.88); }  /* was 0.96 */
  .m-page .sg-overlay-med    { background-color: rgb(15 20 32 / 0.78); }  /* was 0.83 */
  .m-page .sg-overlay-light  { background-color: rgb(15 20 32 / 0.62); }  /* was 0.72 */

  /* E1 - gold contrast floor. After lifting --color-primary to the
     saturated #D4A95C, low-opacity text-primary uses (decorative
     kickers, accent text at /22-/55) need a baseline that still hits
     AA against the new dark base. The hand-tuned RGB values below
     give ~4.7:1 at the lower tier and ~5.5:1 at the mid tier on void;
     full-opacity uses (text-primary, text-primary/60+) need no floor. */
  .m-page :is(.text-primary\/22, .text-primary\/30, .text-primary\/35,
              .text-primary\/38, .text-primary\/40, .text-primary\/42, .text-primary\/45)
  { color: rgb(187 161 121) !important; }
  .m-page :is(.text-primary\/48, .text-primary\/50, .text-primary\/52,
              .text-primary\/55, .text-primary\/58)
  { color: rgb(204 175 121) !important; }

  /* B2 - text contrast floors. Tailwind's text-parchment/N renders as
     color-mix(parchment, transparent, N%). On low-alpha values this drops
     below WCAG AA on the new base; here we lift the floor for the very
     dim opacities the original design used as decorative greys. The hand-
     picked target tiers are primary ≈ #E8EBF0 (~7:1 on new base), secondary
     ≈ #B8C0CC (~4.7:1), tertiary ≈ #8A94A3 (~4.6:1). */
  .m-page :is(.text-parchment\/20, .text-parchment\/22, .text-parchment\/25,
              .text-header-foreground\/20, .text-header-foreground\/22, .text-header-foreground\/25)
  { color: rgb(138 148 163) !important; }
  .m-page :is(.text-parchment\/30, .text-parchment\/35, .text-parchment\/38, .text-parchment\/40,
              .text-header-foreground\/25, .text-header-foreground\/30, .text-header-foreground\/35, .text-header-foreground\/40)
  { color: rgb(155 164 178) !important; }
  .m-page :is(.text-parchment\/42, .text-parchment\/45, .text-parchment\/48, .text-parchment\/50,
              .text-header-foreground\/42, .text-header-foreground\/45, .text-header-foreground\/50)
  { color: rgb(174 182 195) !important; }

  /* B3 - minimum font sizes. Lifts the smallest utility classes used in
     this page so no rendered text falls below 13px. Specificity (0,2,0)
     wins over Tailwind's single-class utilities. */
  .m-page .text-\[10px\] { font-size: 13px !important; letter-spacing: 0.14em; }
  .m-page .text-xs       { font-size: 14px !important; }
  .m-page .text-sm       { font-size: 15px !important; line-height: 1.55; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .m-page .text-sm     { font-size: 16px !important; }
  }
  .m-page .text-base     { font-size: 17px !important; line-height: 1.65; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .m-page .text-base   { font-size: 18px !important; }
  }
  .m-page .text-\[17px\] { font-size: 18px !important; line-height: 1.65; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .m-page .text-\[17px\] { font-size: 19px !important; }
  }
  /* Carousel slide bodies use text-[17px] md:text-lg; lift the md:text-lg too. */
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .m-page .swiper-slide .md\:text-lg { font-size: 20px !important; line-height: 1.65; }
  }

  /* B4 - saturated gold for pull statements only. Applied via the
     .pull-gold class on the specific paragraphs the brief enumerates. */
  .m-page .pull-gold {
    color: #D4A95C;
  }

  /* B5 - pagination dots: larger visual, generous tap target, saturated
     gold active state. The visual lives in ::after so the bullet itself
     can be a 24/28px transparent click target on mobile. !important is
     needed because the existing rules earlier in this block use a direct
     background on the bullet. */
  .m-page .sg-pag {
    padding: 16px 0;
  }
  .m-page .sg-pag .swiper-pagination-bullet {
    position: relative;
    width: 24px !important;
    height: 24px !important;
    margin: 0 5px !important;
    background: transparent !important;
    border-radius: 0 !important;
    opacity: 1 !important;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .m-page .sg-pag .swiper-pagination-bullet::after {
    content: '';
    display: block;
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    background: rgba(232, 235, 240, 0.55);
    transition: width 0.22s ease, height 0.22s ease, background 0.22s ease;
  }
  .m-page .sg-pag .swiper-pagination-bullet:hover::after {
    background: rgba(232, 235, 240, 0.85);
  }
  .m-page .sg-pag .swiper-pagination-bullet-active::after {
    width: 18px;
    height: 14px;
    border-radius: 7px;
    background: #D4A95C;
  }
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .m-page .sg-pag .swiper-pagination-bullet {
      width: 28px !important;
      height: 28px !important;
      margin: 0 6px !important;
    }
    .m-page .sg-pag .swiper-pagination-bullet::after {
      width: 16px;
      height: 16px;
    }
    .m-page .sg-pag .swiper-pagination-bullet-active::after {
      width: 20px;
      height: 16px;
      border-radius: 8px;
    }
  }

  /* B6 / E2 - section H2 minimum sizing. Most H2s already use text-3xl
     md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl (30/36/48); brief target 28-32 mobile and
     40-48 desktop. Mobile 30 is within range. Desktop md=36 is below
     the 40-floor; lift it to 40 at the md breakpoint so tablet-width
     headings hit the brief's lower bound. lg sizing (48) already at
     the top. The two outlier H2s at text-2xl md:text-3xl (24/30) are
     lifted to 28/40 by a more specific rule below. */
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .m-page section h2.font-heading.md\:text-4xl {
      font-size: 40px;
    }
  }
  .m-page section h2.font-heading.text-2xl {
    font-size: 28px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .m-page section h2.font-heading.text-2xl.md\:text-3xl {
      font-size: 40px;
    }
  }

  /* D3 - carousel slide heading sizing. The three card carousels
     (patterns, development, process) all use text-xl md:text-2xl
     lg:text-[26px] for the slide h3, which renders 20/24/26 - small
     for the parental demographic. Lift to 22 mobile, 28 desktop so the
     card title reads as the visual anchor it's meant to be. */
  .m-page .swiper-slide h3.font-heading {
    font-size: 22px !important;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .m-page .swiper-slide h3.font-heading {
      font-size: 28px !important;
    }
  }

  /* D5 - saturated gold for h2 headings. The default text-gold-gradient
     uses muted Sangham brand gold (hsl(42 52% 42%)) which doesn't have
     enough contrast against the new (lifted) dark base. Re-tint the
     gradient inside .m-page to the pull-gold tone for proper visibility.
     Site-wide token untouched. */
  .m-page .text-gold-gradient {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #DBAE5E, #D4A95C, #B88A3C);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    color: transparent;
  }

  /* F7 - safe bottom padding on mobile. The floating WhatsApp CTA
     button sits at bottom-6 (~24px) and is ~48px tall, giving ~72px
     of overlay. Adding 88px bottom padding to the page wrapper on
     mobile ensures the last section's content is never obscured. */
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .m-page { padding-bottom: 88px; }
  }

  /* Scroll margin so sticky nav (if any) doesn't hide booking headings */
  #parental-cal,
  #fit-cal {
    scroll-margin-top: 80px;
  }

  /* About Michael light-surface carousel: dark pagination bullets */
  .m-page .sg-pag-light .swiper-pagination-bullet::after {
    background: rgba(26, 31, 46, 0.25) !important;
  }
  .m-page .sg-pag-light .swiper-pagination-bullet:hover::after {
    background: rgba(26, 31, 46, 0.50) !important;
  }
  .m-page .sg-pag-light .swiper-pagination-bullet-active::after {
    background: #A87C35 !important;
  }
</style>

<BaseLayout
  title="Mentoring for Teenagers (Ages 12 to 17)"
  description="Parent-facing developmental mentorship and reflective counselling for young men in the adolescent years. ASCHP-registered. Online worldwide."
  canonicalURL={canonicalURL}
  image="/images/og-mentoring-adolescents.jpg"
  jsonLd={[...jsonLd, faqJsonLd]}
  minimalNav={true}
  hideStickyBar={true}
  hideFloatingWhatsApp={true}
>
<div class="m-page">

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       1. HERO - Dark Base (bg-void)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="bg-void -mt-[72px] pt-[72px]">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 py-16 md:py-24 max-w-6xl">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[3fr_2fr] gap-12 lg:gap-20 items-center">

        <div class="md:order-1">
          <p class="text-primary/40 text-xs tracking-widest uppercase font-body mb-8">
            Sangham &middot; Online Sessions Worldwide
          </p>
          <h1 class="font-heading text-[40px] sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl text-parchment/95 leading-[1.05] mb-8">
            A Different Kind of Support{' '}<br class="hidden sm:block" /><span class="text-gold-gradient">for the Adolescent Years</span>
          </h1>
          <p class="font-body text-base md:text-lg text-parchment/60 leading-relaxed mb-10 max-w-lg">
            Grounded mentorship and reflective counselling for young men aged 12 to 17. And for the parents trying to support them through it.
          </p>

          <blockquote class="pl-6 border-l-2 border-primary/40 mb-10 pb-10 border-b border-b-parchment/10">
            <p class="font-heading text-2xl md:text-3xl text-parchment/88 leading-snug">
              <span class="block pull-gold">Your son is not broken.</span>
              <span class="block mt-3 text-parchment/78">He may just be unsupported at a stage of life that was never meant to be crossed alone.</span>
            </p>
          </blockquote>

          <div class="space-y-3 font-body text-base text-parchment/60 leading-relaxed mb-10">
            <p>Adolescence has always been a difficult stretch of life.</p>
            <p>What is different now is the world a teenager is moving through. Phones, comparison, online life, conflicting messages about who he is supposed to be, and fewer steady adult relationships outside the home than this stage of life has historically required.</p>
            <p>At this age, parents are still the people who matter most. But often what helps a young person settle into himself is a second trusted adult relationship. Someone outside the family.</p>
            <p>Someone who can meet him with honesty rather than worry, and who does not also carry the weight of being his parent.</p>
            <p>This work exists to provide that relationship.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center gap-5 mb-8">
            <a
              href="#parental-cal"
              class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-8 py-4 bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-gold-light transition-all duration-300 rounded-lg text-sm tracking-wider uppercase font-body font-medium shadow-lg shadow-primary/15"
            >
              Book a Parent Consultation
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7" />
              </svg>
            </a>
            <a href="#fit-cal" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-parchment/60 hover:text-parchment/85 text-sm font-body transition-colors">
              Free 15-Minute Fit Call
              <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7" />
              </svg>
            </a>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-1.5">
            {['ASCHP Registered', 'Online sessions available', 'Based in South Africa', 'Ages 12 to 17'].map((t) => (
              <p class="text-parchment/50 text-xs font-body">{t}</p>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="md:order-2 mt-10 md:mt-0 flex justify-center md:justify-end">
          <div class="w-full max-w-[200px] md:max-w-[230px] lg:max-w-[250px]">
            <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden mb-4 border border-parchment/8">
              <div class="aspect-[4/5] overflow-hidden">
                <Image
                  src={michaelPortrait}
                  alt="Michael Kaplan, ASCHP Registered Wellness Counsellor and developmental mentor for young men aged 12 to 17"
                  class="w-full h-full object-cover object-center"
                  widths={[500, 580, 625]}
                  sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 313px, (min-width: 768px) 288px, 250px"
                  width={1254}
                  height={1254}
                  loading="eager"
                  fetchpriority="high"
                />
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="px-1 mb-3">
              <p class="font-heading text-sm text-parchment/75">Michael Kaplan</p>
              <p class="text-primary/50 text-[11px] font-body tracking-wide mt-0.5 leading-snug">ASCHP Registered Wellness Counsellor</p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5 px-1">
              <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full border border-parchment/10 text-parchment/30 text-[10px] font-body">ASCHP Reg.&nbsp;10559</span>
              <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full border border-parchment/10 text-parchment/30 text-[10px] font-body">RYS&nbsp;300</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       2. CREDIBILITY STRIP
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       3. CREDIBILITY STRIP - Dark Base (bg-header, slightly lighter)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="bg-[#D8DDE8] sg-r3 sg-r3-entry">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 py-16 md:py-20 max-w-5xl">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-12 sm:gap-0 text-center sm:text-left sm:divide-x sm:divide-[#1A1F2E]/10">
        <div class="sm:pr-10 xl:pr-16">
          <p class="font-heading text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-[#A87C35] mb-3 leading-none">10+</p>
          <p class="font-body text-[15px] md:text-[16px] text-[#1A1F2E]/70 leading-relaxed">years working directly with adolescent and young adult men</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sm:px-10 xl:px-16">
          <p class="font-heading text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-[#A87C35] mb-3 leading-none">Hundreds</p>
          <p class="font-body text-[15px] md:text-[16px] text-[#1A1F2E]/70 leading-relaxed">of one-on-one and group sessions facilitated across Cape Town and online</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sm:pl-10 xl:pl-16">
          <p class="font-heading text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-[#A87C35] mb-3 leading-none tracking-tight">Trained under</p>
          <p class="font-body text-[15px] md:text-[16px] text-[#1A1F2E]/70 leading-relaxed">a clinical and forensic psychologist in adolescent developmental work</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       4. SOMETHING IS MISSING - Dark Base (bg-void)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="bg-void">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-28 max-w-5xl">

      <div class="max-w-3xl mb-14">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl text-gold-gradient leading-tight">
          What Parents Are Often Seeing
        </h2>
        <span class="h2-accent"></span>
        <div class="space-y-4 font-body text-base text-parchment/60 leading-relaxed">
          <p>Many parents can sense when something in their son's life is not fully settling, even when nothing dramatic has happened.</p>
          <div class="pl-4 border-l border-parchment/15 space-y-1 py-1 text-parchment/50">
            <p>The signs are usually easy to miss at first.</p>
            <p>A door that stays closed.</p>
            <p>Conversations that used to be easy and no longer are.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Patterns carousel (Swiper) -->
      <div class="mb-14">
        <div class="swiper sg-swiper" id="sw-patterns">
          <div class="swiper-wrapper">
            {patternCards.map((card, i) => (
              <div class="swiper-slide">
                <div class="sg-slide border border-parchment/12 rounded-xl p-8 md:p-12 bg-header/30 flex flex-col">
                  <div class="mb-5">
                    <p class="font-heading text-[32px] md:text-[36px] leading-none pull-gold mb-1 tabular-nums">
                      {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-[11px] md:text-[12px] font-body tracking-[0.18em] uppercase text-primary/55">
                      {i + 1} of {patternCards.length}
                    </p>
                  </div>
                  <h3 class="font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl lg:text-[26px] text-parchment/85 leading-snug mb-6">
                    {card.title}
                  </h3>
                  <p class="font-body text-[17px] md:text-lg text-parchment/62 leading-relaxed flex-1">
                    {card.text}
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mt-6">
          <button id="sw-patterns-prev" class="sg-nav-btn w-10 h-10 rounded-full border border-parchment/20 flex items-center justify-center text-parchment/45 hover:text-parchment/75 hover:border-parchment/40 transition-all" aria-label="Previous pattern">
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 12H5M12 19l-7-7 7-7" /></svg>
          </button>
          <div id="sw-patterns-pag" class="flex-1 flex justify-center sg-pag"></div>
          <button id="sw-patterns-next" class="sg-nav-btn w-10 h-10 rounded-full border border-parchment/20 flex items-center justify-center text-parchment/45 hover:text-parchment/75 hover:border-parchment/40 transition-all" aria-label="Next pattern">
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
          </button>
          <p class="text-parchment/20 text-xs font-body hidden sm:block ml-2">Use arrows to navigate</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4 font-body text-base text-parchment/58 leading-relaxed border-t border-parchment/10 pt-10">
        <p>Much of this is a completely normal part of modern adolescence and will pass on its own.</p>
        <p>But some of it is a signal that a young person does not yet have enough space outside himself to think honestly about what he is going through. Parents can provide a great deal of that space. They cannot always provide all of it.</p>
        <p class="font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl text-parchment/75 leading-snug">This work exists to provide one of those spaces.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-void">
    <Image
      src={mistyValley}
      alt=""
      aria-hidden="true"
      class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover object-center"
      widths={[640, 1024, 1536]}
      sizes="100vw"
      loading="lazy"
    />
    <div class="absolute inset-0 sg-overlay-med"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-[#070B14]/20 via-transparent to-[#070B14]/40"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 container mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-28 max-w-5xl">
      <p class="text-primary/55 text-xs tracking-widest uppercase font-body mb-5">The World Has Changed</p>
      <h2 class="font-heading text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl text-gold-gradient leading-tight max-w-2xl">
        Why Adolescence Feels Different Now
      </h2>
      <span class="h2-accent"></span>

      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-5 font-body text-base text-parchment/62 leading-relaxed">
        <p>Adolescence has always involved uncertainty, mood, and pressure. Those parts are not new.</p>
        <p>What is new is the environment teenagers are growing up inside.</p>
        <p>A generation ago, a young person formed an identity slowly. Family, school, a small group of friends, and the part of town he lived in. That was most of the input.</p>
        <blockquote class="py-12 md:py-16 text-center">
          <span class="block w-14 h-px bg-primary/45 mx-auto mb-7"></span>
          <p class="font-heading text-[1.7rem] md:text-[2.15rem] lg:text-[2.35rem] text-primary/90 italic leading-snug max-w-2xl mx-auto">For most of human history, growing up has happened in small, knowable worlds.</p>
        </blockquote>
        <p>Today, much of that same identity work happens through a phone. Hours of comparison with peers he may never meet. Feeds shaping what feels normal and what does not. Conflicting messages about what it means to be a man arriving from every direction at once.</p>
        <blockquote class="py-12 md:py-16 text-center">
          <span class="block w-14 h-px bg-primary/45 mx-auto mb-7"></span>
          <p class="font-heading text-[1.7rem] md:text-[2.15rem] lg:text-[2.35rem] text-primary/90 italic leading-snug max-w-2xl mx-auto">That is no longer the world he is growing up in.</p>
        </blockquote>
        <p>Most parents can see this happening. Few feel fully equipped to talk about it. The territory simply did not exist when they were the same age.</p>
        <p>This often creates a quiet distance between parents and teenagers that no one intended. Parents worry, set limits, ask questions. Teenagers feel watched, misunderstood, or behind on something they cannot quite name.</p>
        <blockquote class="py-12 md:py-16 text-center">
          <span class="block w-14 h-px bg-primary/45 mx-auto mb-7"></span>
          <p class="font-heading text-[1.7rem] md:text-[2.15rem] lg:text-[2.35rem] text-primary/90 italic leading-snug max-w-2xl mx-auto">Few parents alive today have lived through what their sons are now growing up inside.</p>
        </blockquote>
        <p>A second trusted relationship outside the family can sometimes ease that distance. Not by taking sides, but by giving a young person space to think out loud with someone who understands the world he is actually growing up in.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-void">
    <Image
      src={caveMeditation}
      alt=""
      aria-hidden="true"
      class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover object-center"
      widths={[640, 1024, 1536]}
      sizes="100vw"
      loading="lazy"
    />
    <div class="absolute inset-0 sg-overlay-strong"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 container mx-auto px-6 py-40 md:py-52 max-w-3xl text-center">
      <p class="font-heading text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-parchment/82 leading-tight mb-10 md:mb-12">
        The question is not<br class="hidden sm:block" />{' '}<span class="text-parchment/50">"what is wrong with him?"</span>
      </p>
      <p class="font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl text-parchment/52 leading-snug mb-8">
        Often the better question is
      </p>
      <p class="font-heading text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl pull-gold leading-snug">
        "what has he not yet been given?"
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       6B. PULL QUESTION - Dark Base (bg-void, standalone reframe)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="bg-header text-header-foreground">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-28 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-primary/55 text-xs tracking-widest uppercase font-body mb-5">It Has Always Taken More Than Parents</p>
      <h2 class="font-heading text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl text-gold-gradient leading-tight max-w-2xl">
        Adolescence Was Never Meant To Be Navigated Alone
      </h2>
      <span class="h2-accent"></span>

      <div class="space-y-5 font-body text-base text-header-foreground/64 leading-relaxed">
        <p>For most of human history, the move into adulthood did not happen inside a single household. A young person grew up alongside uncles, older cousins, neighbours, teachers, coaches, and other adults who took an interest in his life. Many of those relationships have quietly disappeared from modern family life.</p>
        <p>What remains is the parent or parents.</p>
        <p>One or two adults trying to be everything a teenager needs, at the age where he is also pulling away. Protector. Authority. The person who notices the mood at dinner. The person who knows the homework deadlines. That is a great deal for any family to hold.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="font-heading text-2xl md:text-3xl pull-gold leading-snug max-w-2xl border-y border-header-foreground/10 py-10 my-12">
        Another grounded adult relationship does not replace the role of a parent.
        <span class="block text-header-foreground/72 mt-3">Often it strengthens it.</span>
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-5 font-body text-base text-header-foreground/64 leading-relaxed">
        <p>A teenager will sometimes say things to a trusted outside adult that he is not ready to say at home. Not because the parent has failed. Because the relationship with a parent carries history, dependence, and the weight of being known, all of which a teenager is in the middle of working out.</p>
        <p>A second relationship gives him somewhere to put the parts of himself he is still figuring out. The parent gets to stay the parent.</p>
        <p class="font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl text-header-foreground/78 leading-snug">This work exists to help provide one of those relationships.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       7. A DIFFERENT WAY OF UNDERSTANDING - Register 3 (pale blue-grey)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="how-it-works" class="relative overflow-hidden bg-void">
    <Image
      src={documentaryWaterfall}
      alt=""
      aria-hidden="true"
      class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover object-center"
      widths={[640, 1024, 1536]}
      sizes="100vw"
      loading="lazy"
    />
    <div class="absolute inset-0 sg-overlay-strong"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-[#070B14]/30 via-transparent to-[#070B14]/50"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 container mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-28 max-w-5xl">
      <p class="text-primary/55 text-xs tracking-widest uppercase font-body mb-5">The Process</p>
      <h2 class="font-heading text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl text-gold-gradient leading-tight max-w-2xl">
        What The Mentorship Offers
      </h2>
      <span class="h2-accent"></span>

      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4 font-body text-base text-parchment/62 leading-relaxed mb-12">
        <p>Every teenager arrives different. Different temperament, different family, different version of what is hard.</p>
        <p>The mentorship is shaped around the individual young person, inside a steady structure of consistency, honesty, and reflection.</p>
        <p class="font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl text-parchment/82 leading-snug border-l-2 border-primary/42 pl-5">The relationship itself is part of the work.</p>
        <p>Many teenagers have very few places where they can think out loud without being judged, corrected, or asked what they are going to do about it. That space is most of what is missing.</p>
        <p>Over time, having one steady relationship of that kind can help a young person slow down enough to think honestly about himself, the pressures he is moving through, and the kind of person he is becoming.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-14">
        <div class="swiper sg-swiper" id="sw-process">
          <div class="swiper-wrapper">
            {processStages.map((stage) => (
              <div class="swiper-slide">
                <div class="sg-slide border border-parchment/15 rounded-xl p-8 md:p-12 bg-header/30 flex flex-col">
                  <div class="flex items-start gap-4 mb-6">
                    <span class="font-heading text-[32px] md:text-[40px] pull-gold leading-none shrink-0 tabular-nums">
                      {stage.stage}
                    </span>
                    <h3 class="font-heading text-xl md:text-2xl lg:text-[26px] text-parchment/88 leading-snug pt-1">
                      {stage.title}
                    </h3>
                  </div>
                  <p class="font-body text-[17px] md:text-lg text-parchment/65 leading-relaxed flex-1">
                    {stage.text}
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mt-6">
          <button id="sw-process-prev" class="sg-nav-btn w-10 h-10 rounded-full border border-parchment/22 flex items-center justify-center text-parchment/45 hover:text-parchment/75 hover:border-parchment/45 transition-all" aria-label="Previous">
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 12H5M12 19l-7-7 7-7" /></svg>
